hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8251","8299 Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdul-Razzaq told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Kuhayl, he said: Zayd Ibn Wahb told us that he was in the army who were with Ali who marched against the Kharijites, so Ali said: “O People, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: A people from my nation will emerge reciting the Qur’an, and your recitation will not be equivalent to their recitation. Nothing, nor is your prayer comparable to their prayer, nor is your fasting anything comparable to their fasting. They recite the Qur’an, thinking that it is theirs, but it is against them. Their prayer will go beyond their necks, they will leave Islam as an arrow leaves a target. If only you knew the army they will strike, what has been decreed for them. On the tongue of their Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, do not be weary of work, and the sign of that is that among them is a man who has an upper arm but no arm, at the head of His upper arm is like the nipple of a woman’s breast, with white hairs on it. Salamah said: So Zaid descended upon me, house by house, until we passed a bridge, on The Kharijites Abdullah bin Wahb Al-Rasibi, and he said to them: Throw down your spears and draw your swords from their hilts, for I fear that they will appeal to you. He said: So they unsheathed their swords and lowered their hilts, and the people attacked them, meaning with their spears, and they killed one of them against one another, and not a single person was struck on that day except Two men. Ali said: They searched among them for the newborn, but they did not find him. So Ali himself rose until he came to people, killing one another. He said: They stripped them, and they found him near the earth, so Ali said the takbir and said: God has spoken the truth, and he has conveyed the message, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so Ubaidah Al-Salmani rose to him, He said: O Commander of the Faithful, by God, there is no god but Him. I heard this hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Yes, by God There is no god but Him. I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he made him swear three times, and he swears to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8252","8300 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: Ali said: “ Had you not been reckless, I would have informed you of what God had promised to those who would kill them on the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: You heard it from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8253","8301 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: Muhammad bin Sirin told us, he said: Ubaidah Al-Salmani said: When he was where the people of the river were injured, he said: Ali said: “Seek among them, for if they are the people who The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned them. Among them was a man with a jointed hand, or a clubbed hand, or a flexed hand. So we followed him. So we found him, so we showed him to him, and when he saw him, he said: God is the greatest, God is the greatest, God is the greatest. He said: By God, had you not been quick to do so, Then he mentioned a word that means, “I have told you about what God has decreed on the tongue of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for those who were responsible for killing these people.” I said: You. Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaaba, three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8254","8302 Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad informed us, saying: Abu Malik Amr, who is Ibn Hashim, told us on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Abi Khaled, he said: Amr bin Qays told me, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, that he heard Ali say: “I gouged out the eye of Sedition, and had it not been for me, the people of Nahrawan would not have been killed, and had it not been that I fear that you will abandon your work, I would have informed you of what God had decreed on the authority of Your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was for those he fought, seeing their error, knowing the guidance that we follow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8255","'Amr ibn 'Ali al-Fallas said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi al-'Anbari narrated to us, saying: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar al-'Ajali narrated to me, saying: Abu Zumayl narrated to me, saying: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas narrated to me, saying:\n\n\When the Khawarij (al-Haruriyyah) rebelled"," they secluded themselves in a house"," numbering six thousand. I said to 'Ali: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," hold back the prayer a while"," so that I might speak to these people.' He said: 'I fear for you from them.' I said: 'No.' So I dressed"," combed my hair"," and entered upon them in the house at midday while they were eating. They said: 'Welcome to you"," O Ibn 'Abbas! What has brought you to us?' I said to them: 'I have come to you from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ — the Muhajirun and the Ansar — and from the Prophet's ﷺ cousin and son-in-law"," upon whom the Qur'an was revealed. They are more knowledgeable of its interpretation than you"," and none of them are among you. I shall convey to you what they say"," and convey to them what you say.' A group of them stepped aside for me. I said: 'Tell me what you find against the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ companions and his cousin.' They said: 'Three things.' I said: 'What are they?' He said: 'As for one of them: it is men passing judgment in the matter of Allah"," while Allah says: Judgment belongs to none but Allah. What have men to do with judgment?' I said: 'That is one.' He said: 'As for the second: he fought but did not revile"," and did not take spoils. If they were disbelievers"," their enslavement would be lawful; and if they were believers"," neither their enslavement nor their fighting would be lawful.' I said: 'That is two. What is the third?' — and he mentioned a word to the effect that — they said: 'He has erased himself from the title of Commander of the Faithful. If he is not the Commander of the Faithful"," then he is the Commander of the Disbelievers.' I said: 'Do you have anything other than this?' They said: 'This suffices us.'\n\nI said to them: 'Have you considered — if I recite to you from the Book of Allah"," Glorified and Exalted is He"," and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ"," that which refutes your statement — will you return?' They said: 'Yes.'\n\nI said: 'As for your statement that men pass judgment in the matter of Allah: I recite to you from the Book of Allah that He has placed judgment among men concerning the value of a quarter-dirham"," and Allah"," Blessed and Exalted"," commanded that they judge by it. Have you considered the words of Allah"," Blessed and Exalted: O you who believe"," do not kill game while in ihram; whoever kills it intentionally shall recompense with the like of what he has killed from livestock — to be judged by two just men among you. And it was part of Allah's judgment that He delegated it to men who judge by it. Had He willed"," He would have judged by it Himself. So it is permissible for men to pass judgment. I adjure you by Allah: is men's judgment in reconciling between people and preventing bloodshed better"," or in a rabbit?' They said: 'Yes"," this is better.' And regarding the woman and her husband: And if you fear dissension between them"," send an arbitrator from his people and an arbitrator from her people. I adjure you by Allah: is men's judgment in reconciling between them and preventing bloodshed better than their judgment over the intimate part of a woman?' I said: 'Have I brought you out of this?' They said: 'Yes.'\n\nI said: 'As for your statement — he fought but did not revile and did not take spoils — do you revile your mother 'Aishah"," and is that which is unlawful with other women lawful with her"," while she is your mother? If you say: We consider lawful with her what we consider lawful with others"," then you have disbelieved. And if you say: She is not our mother"," then you have disbelieved. The Prophet ﷺ is more deserving of the believers than their own selves"," and his wives are their mothers. So you are between two misguidances. Find a way out of this. Have I brought you out of this?' They said: 'Yes.'\n\nAs for your saying that he erased himself from the title of Commander of the Faithful: we shall bring you what satisfies you — that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ"," on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah"," made peace with the polytheists and said to 'Ali: \""Write"," O 'Ali: This is what Muhammad"," the Messenger of Allah"," has made peace upon.\"" They said: 'Did we know that you were the Messenger of Allah"," we would not have fought you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Erase"," O 'Ali. O Allah"," You know that I am the Messenger of Allah. Erase"," O 'Ali"," and write: This is what Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah has made peace upon.' By Allah"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than 'Ali"," and he erased himself"," and his erasing himself did not erase him from Prophethood. Have I brought you out of this?' They said: 'Yes.'\n\nTwo thousand of them returned"," and the rest went out and were killed upon their misguidance"," killed by the Muhajirun and the Ansar.\"""""
"8256","8304 Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Saleh told us, he said: Amr bin Hashim al-Janabi told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Alqamah Ibn Qais, he said: I said to Ali: “You shall put a distance between you and the son of the liver-eaters.” As an arbitrator? He said: I was the writer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hudaybiyyah, and he wrote: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, agreed upon. And Suhail bin Amr, and Suhail said: If we had known that he was the Messenger of God, we would not have fought him. Erase it. So I said: He, by God, is the Messenger of God. Against your will, no, by God, I will not erase it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, Show me its place. So I showed him and he erased it, and said: As for yours, Like it, and you are forced.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8257","8305 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Baraa, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made peace with the people of Hudaybiyyah, and Ibn Bashar said: The people of Mecca wrote to Ali A letter was written between them. He said: So Muhammad, the Messenger of God, wrote. Then the polytheists said: Do not write Muhammad is the Messenger of God. If you were the Messenger of God, we would not fight you. He said Ali: Erase it. He said: I am not the one who erased it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, erased it with his hand, so he made peace with them on the condition that he would enter. He stayed with his companions for three days, and he did not enter it except by bringing weapons. So I asked him. Ibn Bashar said: They asked him, “What is it that brings weapons?” He said: “With what.” \in it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8258","8306 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Umrah in Dhul-Qa’dah, but the people of Mecca refused to let him enter Mecca, even He judged them on the condition that he would stay there for three days. When they wrote the letter, they wrote: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, judged. They said: We do not acknowledge it. If we had known that you are the Messenger of God, we would not have prevented you from his house, but you are Muhammad bin Abdullah. He said: I am the Messenger of God, and I am Muhammad bin Abdullah. He said to Ali: Erase the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: By God, I will never erase you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the letter. He is not good at writing, so he wrote in the place of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Muhammad, so he wrote: This is what Muhammad bin Abdullah decided upon, no. He may enter Mecca with any weapon except the sword in a bag, and he may not expel anyone from its people if he wants to follow him, and he must not prevent any of his companions. If he wanted to stay, then when he entered it and the time had passed, they came to Ali and said: Tell your companion to leave us, for the time had passed, so he left. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Hamza’s daughter followed him, calling: O uncle, O uncle. So Ali handed it to her, took it in her hand, and said: To Fatima: “Better than you is your cousin.” So she carried her, and Ali, Zaid, and Ja’far disputed over her, and Ali said: I will take her, and she is my cousin. Ja`far said: My cousin, and her paternal aunt is below me. Zayd said: My brother’s daughter, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that she should go to her maternal aunt. And he said: The aunt is in the same position as the mother. Then he said to Ali: You are from me, and I am from you. And he said to Jafar, you resemble me in character and character. Then he said To Zaid: You are our brother and our master. Ali said: Won’t you marry Hamza’s daughter? He said: She is my foster-brother’s daughter. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8259","8307 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is the son of Adam, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of my father Ishaq, on the authority of Hani ibn Hani, and Hubayra ibn Yarim, on the authority of Ali, “They disputed about the daughter of Hamza, and the Messenger of God decided for her.” May God bless him and grant him peace to her paternal aunt, and he said: The maternal aunt is a mother. I said: O Messenger of God, won’t you marry her? He said: She is not permissible for me. She is My brother’s daughter through breastfeeding. He said to Ali: You are from me, and I am from you. He said to Zaid: You are our brother and our protector. He said to Ja’far: You resemble me. “My character and my character” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8260","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Khalid told us, saying: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He walked to Badr, so he consulted the Muslims, then Abu Bakr advised him, then he consulted them, so Omar advised him, then he consulted them, so she said Al-Ansar: O community of Ansar, beware of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wants. They said: Then we will not say, what the Children of Israel said to Moses: Go, you and your Lord, and fight. Here we are sitting. By the One who has sent you with the truth, if you were to strike the livers of camels to Burk al-Ghimad, We will not follow you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8261","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: And Muammar confirmed me, after on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubair, that Maswar bin Makhramah and Marwan bin Al-Hakam, one of them adding to the other, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out. He went to Al-Hudaybiyyah with some ten hundred of his companions. When Dhul-Hulayfah came, he imitated the sacrificial animal, made it combed, and entered ihram from her. Then he He sent an eye for him from Khuza’ah, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked on until, when he was mentioning a word in a vague way, his eye came to him, and they said: Indeed The Quraysh gathered a group for you, and they gathered for you the Abyssinians, and they were fighting you, and they turned you away from the House. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Admonish me.” Do you think that we should look after the descendants of these people who have helped us? If they survive, God will have cut off the neck of the infidels. Otherwise, Did you leave them fighting and dying? Then Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, I only went out for this purpose, intending for this house. You do not want to fight. Uhud, so he turned to him, and whoever turned us away from him, we fought him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Proceed in the name of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8262","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Da’eef told me, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Visible between two shields on the day of Uhud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8263","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim reported, saying: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He entered the year of conquest with the forgiven on his head. When he took it off, a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, Ibn Khatal is attached to With the curtains of the Kaaba, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8264","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: I wrote to Nafi’: Can a man get pregnant without the prince’s permission? He said: He does not carry anything except with His permission. He said: And what you wrote asking me about the invasion, did you hear from Ibn Umar about it, that the people were being called to Islam at the beginning of Islam, before the fighting? And Ibn Umar told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “raid against Banu al-Mustaliq, meaning: Khuza’ah, and they were raiding. And their livestock were watered by the water, so he killed their men, took their captives captive, and took their livestock.” So that was the day on which he struck Juwayriyah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8265","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ali bin Ubaid told us, saying: Idris Al-Awdi told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent as an emir over a people, he would order him to fear God especially for himself. And to his companions in general, and he said: “Fight in the name of God, and in the cause of God, fight those who disbelieve in God, and do not go to extremes, do not deceive, and do not mutilate.” And do not kill a newborn, and if you meet your enemy among the polytheists, invite them to one of three things: to Islam, and if they enter into Islam, So accept from them, and desist from them and until the migration. If they enter the migration, then accept from them, and desist from them, even if they choose. They embraced Islam and refused to move from their homes to the place of migration. They were like the Bedouins of the believers. What happens to the Bedouins applies to them. Believers, and they do not have anything of the spoils or spoils, unless they strive in the cause of God. If they refuse to accept Islam, then invite them to give tribute, and accept from them, and desist from them. If they refuse, seek help from God and fight them. If you besiege the people of a fortress, then They wanted you to bring them down according to the rule of God, so do not put them down, but according to your rule, then judge them after whatever you wish, for you do not You do not know whether you will carry out God’s ruling or not, and if they want you to put them under the protection of God and the protection of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, then do not put them down. But your obligations and the obligations of your fathers and brothers, for you to conceal your obligations and the obligations of your fathers and brothers is easier for you than to “Fear the pledge of God and the pledge of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8266","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: Sahl bin Sa’d told me, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said on the Day of Khaybar: “Tomorrow I will give this banner to a man at whose hands God will grant victory, who loves God and His Messenger, and God loves him.” And His Messenger.” When the morning came, the people went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of them hoping to be given it. He said: “Where is Ali bin Abi?” “A student?” Then it was said: He, O Messenger of God, has an eye problem. So they sent for him, and he was brought. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spat in his mouth. His eyes, and prayed for him, and he was healed as if he had no ailment, so he gave him the standard, and Ali said: O Messenger of God, I will fight them until they are Like us? He said: “Continue with your messengers until you arrive at their place, then invite them to Islam, and inform them of what is obligatory upon them according to God’s right in it. By God, for God to guide a man through you is better for you than to have red camels.”"
"8267","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Suleiman bin Harb reported, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He entered upon a Jewish boy who was sick, and he said to him: “Peace be upon him.” He looked at his father, and his father said to him: Obey the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Praise be to God. who saved him from the fire through me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8268","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Hilal told me Ibn Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yassar, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, who said: I had a female servant who took care of my sheep in the presence of Uhud. And the interior, so I looked at it carefully, and behold, the wolf had taken a sheep from it, and I from the children of Adam are sorry as they are, but I am I minted it in a real form, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him, and that was very difficult for me. I said: Shall I not free her, O Messenger of God? The Prophet said to her: “Who am I?” She said: You are the Messenger of God. He said to her: “Where is God?” She said: In heaven. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And in This hadith, he said: “Free her, for she is a believing woman,” and I did not understand it the way I wanted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8269","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he heard Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He caught The Muslims saw a man among his spoils, and he said: Peace be upon you. So they killed him and took his spoils. Then God Almighty revealed: And do not say to him who threw Peace be upon you. You are not a believer. You seek the reward of the life of this world. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8270","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Adi bin Al-Khayyar, on the authority of Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad, that he told him, that he said: O Messenger of God, what if I met a man from the infidels, and he fought me? He struck one of my hands with a sword and cut it off, then he took refuge from me by a tree and said: I have submitted to God. Should I kill him, O Messenger of God, after I... He said it? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not kill him.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, he cut off my hand. Then he said: That was after He cut it, should I kill him? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not kill him, for if you do kill him, he will be in the position you were before you killed him, and you In his position before he said the word he said."
"8271","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: Ayoub told me, he said: Abu Qalaba told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that Thaqif was allies of Banu Aqil in pre-Islamic times, so the Muslims attacked a man from Banu Aqil, and he had his she-camel with him, so they came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, for what did you take me and Sa’ibat al-Hajj? He said: “I took Thaqif for the crime of your allies.” They had captured two Muslim men, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was passing by while he was imprisoned. Then he says: O Muhammad, I am a Muslim. He said: “If I had said, ‘And you are in control of your affairs,’ you would have been completely successful.” Then the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, it seemed to him that he would ransom him with the Thaqafi, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ransomed two Muslim men, and he captured The camel for himself (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8272","Ahmad bin Yahya al-Kufi al-Sufi told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, He said: We came to Bishr bin Asim Al-Laythi, and he said: Uqba bin Malik told us, and he was from his group. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent He delivered a group, and it raided a people, and a man from among the people strayed, so a man from the company followed him, who had a drawn sword, and the aberrant among the people said: I am a Muslim, but he did not look at what he said, so he struck him and killed him. Then the hadith reached the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said something about it. Severe, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering a sermon, when the killer said: By God, he was not the one, he said: except to seek refuge from killing. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him and from the people before him, and he began his sermon, then he said: O Messenger of God, By God, he did not say: He who said: Except that he sought refuge from killing, so he turned away from it, and he turned from the people before him, and he began his sermon, and was not patient. On the third occasion, he said something like that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached him. The displeasure on his face was evident, and he said: “Indeed, God refuses.” On the one who killed a believer three times.”"
"8273","Muhammad ibn Adam al-Musaysi informed me, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Usama ibn Zayd, he said: “We sent The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Al-Harqat from Juhayna, so we went to them in the morning and they had approached us, so we went out in their tracks, so I overtook them. A man, so when I caught up with him, he said: There is no god but God. I thought he was saying it as a weapon, so I attacked him and killed him, so he appeared in I was worried about something about him, so I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to me: “Did he say there is no god but God, and then you killed him?” ! I said: He did not say it himself, but rather said it as a group of weapons. He said to me: “He said there is no god but Allah, and then you killed him?” ! So, will you not open his heart so that you know that he only said it as a weapon? ! \"," Osama said: He kept repeating it to me: \""He said there is no god but Allah and then you killed him? ! “So much so that I wished I had not converted to Islam"," except on that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8274","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, he said I heard Usama bin Zaid saying: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with an army to the Harqat neighborhood of Juhayna, and when he meant we defeated them, A man from the Ansar and I went to meet a man from among them, and he said: There is no god but God. The Ansar stopped him, and I thought that he had only said it. I sought refuge, so I killed him. Then Al-Ansari returned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he told him the hadith. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Osama, you killed a man after he said: There is no god but God. How will you do, “There is no god but God on the Day of Resurrection.” And he still said that I wish I had not converted to Islam, except on that day. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8275","Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumsi reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar reported, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He sent The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attributed Khalid bin Al-Walid to Banu Khuzaymah, but they did not do well to say: We have submitted to Islam, so they did so. They say: We were young, we were young, and Khaled made killing and captivity among them. He said: So he gave to each man of us his captive, until the day came Khaled ordered us that each man of us kill his prisoner. Ibn Omar said: So I said: By God, I will not kill my prisoner, nor will he kill a man of my companions. His captive, he said: So we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned to him the good deed of Khalid, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh God, I “I absolve you of the good deed of Khaled” twice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8276","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Sulaiman bin Harb narrated, he said: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God prayed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Khaybar, he performed the morning prayer with a seat, while he was close to them, so he attacked them and said: “God is great, Khaybar has been ruined. Twice, “When we camped in a people’s place, the morning of those who had been given warnings had become dark.” He said: “And they started running on the highways, saying: Muhammad and Thursday.” Muhammad and Al-Khamis, Muhammad and Al-Khamis, twice, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed the female fighter, and took the offspring captive, and Safiyya became To Dihya al-Kalbi, then she later went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he freed her, married her, and made her emancipation his dowry. Abdul Aziz said: O Abu Muhammad, you are the one who said to Anas: How true is she? Anas said: She told the truth herself, so Thabit moved his head, meaning he believed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8277","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Khaybar and came to it at night, and whenever he came to a people at night, he would not attack them until the morning. So the Jews went out with their sacks and tents, and when they saw him, they said: Muhammad, by God, Muhammad and Al-Khamis, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allah is the Greatest. Khaybar has been destroyed. When we camped in a people’s battlefield, the morning of those who had been warned would be bad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8278","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Abbas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged Al-Taif,” brief."
"8279","Muhammad bin Bashar narrated, saying: Muhammad bin Ja’far narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Maymun Abi Abdullah, that Abdullah bin Buraydah He told him, on the authority of Buraydah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will give the standard to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God loves him.” And His Messenger.” So he called Ali while he was gray-haired, spit in his eyes, gave him the banner, and some of the people got up with him and met the people of Khaybar. Then, Marhab trembles and says: Khaybar has learned that I am Marhab, wielding weapons, a tried and tested hero. Sometimes I stab, and sometimes I strike. Lo! It came blazing, so he and Ali differed in blows, and he struck him on the crown of his head until the sword bit through it, and his head turned white, and the people of The army heard the sound of its blow, so God gave victory to him and to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8280","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb told us, he said: Muadh bin Khaled told us, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraydah, he said: I heard Abu Buraidah saying: We besieged Khaybar, so he took the general, Abu Bakr, and he left, and it was not opened for him, and Omar took him the next day. So he left, and it was not opened for him, and the people were beset by hardship and distress on that day, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will defend my banner tomorrow.” To a man whom God and His Messenger love, and who loves God and His Messenger, he will not return until the victory is opened for him. “And we will sleep comfortably, for our souls, for the victory will be tomorrow.” So when In the morning the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the morning prayer, then he stood up and called for the banner, and the people were in their ranks, but not one of us was a person for him. He was of high status with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he hoped to be the bearer of the standard. So he called Ali bin Abi Talib, who was an armour-wielding man. Then he spit in his eyes, wiped it off, and handed the banner to him, so God opened the door for him. He said: “I am among those for whom you are insulting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8281","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: He is Abu Awanah, Al-Waffah told us, he said: Yahya told us He is Ibn Abi Sulaym Abu Balj. He said: Amr bin Maymun told us that Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will send a man who loves God and His Messenger, God and His Messenger love him, God will never disgrace him, so he is more honorable than he who is honorable.” He said: “Where is Ali?” And he was Ibn Abi Talib? While he was in the mill grinding, he called him while he was so gray that he could hardly see, so he blew on his eyes and shook the banner three times. So he gave her to him, and he brought Safiyya bint Huyay. Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8282","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said On the Day of Khaybar: “I will give this banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God will grant him victory.” Omar bin Al-Khattab said: I did not like the emirate. Except on that day, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Ali bin Abi Talib, gave it to him, and said: “Go, and do not turn around until it opens.” May God be upon you.” Ali walked for a while, then stopped, and Qutiba mentioned a word that meant it, so he shouted: O Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, according to what I fight people? He said: “Fight them until they bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. If they do that, their blood will be spared from you. And their wealth is only due to what is due to it, and their reckoning is with Allah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8283","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Wahb reported, he said: My father told us, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abi Yaqoub speaking, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an army and appointed Zayd bin Haritha against them, and said: “If he is killed Zaid, or he is martyred, then your prince is Ja’far bin Abi Talib, and if Ja’far is killed or martyred, then your prince is Abdullah bin Rawahah.” So they met the enemy, and Zayd took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Jafar took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Abdullah bin Abdullah took the banner. Rawaha, and he fought until he was killed, then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner, so God gave him victory, and news of them came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, So he went out to the people, thanked God and praised Him, then said: “Your brothers have met the enemy, so Zaid bin Haritha took the banner and fought.” Until he was killed or martyred, then Ja`far took the banner, and he fought until he was killed or martyred, then Abdullah bin Rawaha took the banner, So he fought until he was killed or martyred, then Khaled ibn al-Walid, one of the swords of God, took the banner, and God granted victory to him. Then the family of Ja`far gave three periods of respite. To come to them. Then he came to them and said: Do not cry over my brother after today. Then he said: Call for me my brother’s children. So we were brought as if we were chicks. He said: “Call the barber for me.” So he ordered him to shave our heads, then he said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib, and as for Abdullah, he resembles my character. And my character, then he took my hand and tied it up, and said: “O God, replace Ja’far in his family, and bless Abdullah in the pledge of his oath,” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8284","Ahmad bin Sulaiman narrated, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi narrated to us, he said: Saeed narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Anas “Ibn Umm Maktum had a black flag of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with him in some of the scenes of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8285","And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya’qub Al-Thaqafi narrated to me, he said: Yunus bin narrated to me. Ubaid, a servant of Muhammad bin Al-Qasim, said: Muhammad bin Al-Qasim sent me to Al-Bara bin Azib, to ask him about the banner of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, what was it? He said: “It was black, square, of a number.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8286","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Salam Abu Al-Mundhir told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hassan, he said: “I entered the mosque, and suddenly the mosque was crowded with people, and then there was a black flag. I said: What is the matter with the people today? They said: This is it.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to send Amr ibn al-Aas as a leader.”"
"8287","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, burned the palm trees of Bani Al-Nadir and cut it, which is the buairah, so God revealed: Whatever linah you cut or leave standing on its roots. He said: The linah is the palm tree. So, by God’s permission, may He disgrace the transgressors.”"
"8288","Abdul Rahman bin Khalid told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “burned and cut down the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir,” and Hassan says to her: “There is a fire on the battlefields of Banu Luayy like a spreading bush.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8289","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated on the authority of Affan Al-Saffar, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, he said: Habib bin Abi Amra narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, regarding God’s saying: “Whatever palm tree you cut or leave standing on its roots,” He said: “The palm tree is the palm tree.” And to shame the transgressors. He said: “They brought them down from their fortresses and ordered the palm trees to be cut down.” Their hearts itched, so the Muslims said: We have cut down Some, and we left some, so we will ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is there any reward for us for what we have given, and what we owe for what we have left behind? A burden? Then God Almighty revealed: Whatever you cut down or leave standing. Al-Zaafrani said: Affan narrated this hadith to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid, on the authority of Habib, then he came back and we narrated to him on the authority of Hafs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8290","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad Abu Omar Al-Harrani reported, saying: Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Muhammad bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Khathami, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever cuts a sidra... “God set his head in the fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8291","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, he said: I heard Jarir saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Isn’t that khalasa enough for me?” I said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who is not steadfast on horses, so he comforted me and said: “O God, make him steadfast. And make him a guide, a true guide.” He said: “So I went out with fifty of my people, so I went to it and we burned it.” Sufyan said another time: So I went to it. So I burned it, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: By God, I did not come to you until you left it like a mangy camel. So he called for Ahmose. Her horses and her men (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8292","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If you find so-and-so and so-and-so belonging to two men from Quraysh, burn them with fire.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said When we wanted to leave, he said: “Indeed, I ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so, and no one punishes with fire except Allah. So if you find them, So kill them.”"
"8293","Abu Asim reported, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad Kufi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah On the authority of his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we passed by the village of Naml that had been burned. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “It is not appropriate for a human being to be tortured with the punishment of God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8294","Qutaibah bin Saeed narrated, saying: Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, and Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman narrated, saying: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “A prophet from the prophets descended under a tree, and an ant stung him. He ordered his departure, and he was taken out from under it, then burned.” On the ants its village, so God revealed to him: Bring one ant. And Qutaibah said in his hadith: Then an ant stung him, so he ordered it to be prepared. So he took it out from under it, then he ordered it to be burned, so God inspired it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8295","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Al-Aswad bin Saree’ told us, he said: We were in They invaded us, so we defeated them, and we killed among the polytheists, until their killing reached the point where they killed offspring, so that reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he said: “What is the matter with people whose killing has reached the point of killing offspring?! Will not offspring be killed? Will not offspring be killed?” It was said: Why, O Messenger of God, are they not the children of the polytheists? He said: “Aren’t the best among you the children of the polytheists?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8296","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail, who is Ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Yazid, he said: كَتَبَ نَجْدَةُ إِلَى ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ ، يَسْأَلُهُ عَنْ قَتْلِ الْوِلْدَانِ ، وَعَنْ ذِي الْقُرْبَى ، وَعَنِ الْيَتِيمِ مَتَى يَنْقَضِي يُتْمُهُ ، وَعَنِ The male and female slave attending the conquest, do they have a share in it? Ibn Abbas said: “If he had not fallen into foolishness, I would not have answered him. Write, O Yazid: You wrote asking about children. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He did not kill them, so do not kill them, unless you know from them what the companion of Moses knew. As for the relatives, So we claim that we are they, but our people refuse that, and as for the orphan, his orphanage is ended if he reaches the sense of maturity from him, and as for the slave And the woman, they have nothing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8297","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who told him that a woman was found in one of the raids of the Messenger of God. She was killed, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, denounced the killing of women and children.”"
"8298","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, he said: Ibn Wahb reported, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Atiya A man from Banu Qurayzah told him, “The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Qurayzah stripped him, and when they did not see the razor, it ran.” On his pubic hair, they spared him from being killed.”"
"8299","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Atiya al-Qurazi, he said: “I was among those who ruled There was happiness in it, so he brought me, and I thought that he was going to kill me, so they discovered my pubic hair, and they found that I had not succumbed, so they put me in captivity.”"
"8300","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, he said: Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said: I heard Atiya al-Qurazi, He says: “We presented it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Qurayzah, and whoever produced it was killed, and whoever did not produce it was let go, and I was among those who He did not grow, so let me go.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8301","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri Al-Basri narrated, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri and Al-Harith bin narrated to us. Poor person, the reading of it, and the pronunciation of it, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the polytheists of the house spending the night, and some of their wives and offspring would be afflicted. He said: “They are one of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8302","Yusuf bin Saeed Al-Masisi and Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi reported, and the pronunciation of it, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Juraij said: He told me Amr bin Dinar, that Ibn Shihab told him, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab bin Jathama, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was told: What if horses raided at night and killed some of the sons of the polytheists? He said: “They are from their fathers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8303","Muhammad bin Al-Ala reported, he said: Ibn Idris reported, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Saab Bin Juthama, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There is no fever except for God and His Messenger,” and he was asked about the people spending the night. They infect the children. He said: “They are among them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8304","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Hisham bin Abdul Malik told us, he said: Omar bin Murqa’ bin Saifi bin Rabah bin told us, Rabi’, who said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of his grandfather, Rabah ibn Rabi’, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a battle, and the people They gathered about something, so he sent a man and said: “See what these people gathered for?” So he came and said: About a woman who had been killed, so he said: “What was it?” “This woman is fighting, and Khaled bin Al-Walid is in the lead.” He said: “Say to Khalid: Do not kill his offspring or a violent man.”"
"8305","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Murqa’, on the authority of his grandfather Rabah bin Al-Rabi’, he said: We were with the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in a secret, with Khalid bin Al-Walid leading it, so we passed by a murdered woman from among the things that happened to the leading one. So we stood looking at it and marveling at it, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came riding his camel, so we separated from her, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This woman was not fighting.” Then he looked into the faces of the people and said to a man among them: “Come to Khalid. So say to him: Do not kill any offspring or a violent person.”"
"8306","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, and the wording is Amr’s, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, who said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Murqa’ bin Saifi, on the authority of Hanzala al-Mukatib, said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and we passed by a woman who had been killed and people... So they went out to him, and he said: “This woman did not fight. Truth is eternal, so tell him: Do not kill his offspring or a violent man.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8307","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad reported, saying: Omar bin Hafs told us, saying: My father told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: When we met on the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed, and I did not see anyone chanting. Truly for him, it is more severe than the appeal of Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to his Lord Almighty, while he says: “O God, I seek Your promise. And your promise, O God, I ask you for what you promised me, O God, if this group is destroyed, you will not be worshiped on earth.” Then he turned to us, and as if The moon made his face slit, and he said: “These are the people’s evening pastures.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8308","Abduh bin Abdullah reported, he said: Suwayd reported, on the authority of Zuhair, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Bara, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the Day of Khaybar, Abu Sufyan was leading him on the Day of Khaybar, while he was on his white mule. He came down and asked for victory, then he said: “I am the Prophet, I am not lying. Ibn Abdul Muttalib\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8309","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Azhar bin al-Qasim al-Makki told us, saying: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded, he would say: “O God, you are my support and my helper, and by you I fight.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8310","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Abdullah bin Qays, on the authority of Abu Musa, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he feared a people, would say: “O God, we place you in their presence, and we seek refuge in protect you from their evils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8311","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the Day of the Trench, he said: “O God, who sent down the Book, who is quick to judge, who sends down the clouds, defeat them and shake them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8312","Muhammad bin Uthman reported, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Suhaib, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to move his lips during the days of Hunayn after the dawn prayer. They said: O Messenger of God, you are moving your lips. With something? He said: “Indeed, a prophet who was before you, then he mentioned a word that pleased him because of the large size of his nation, and he said: No one will be pleased with these people.” something, so God revealed to him, “Give your nation a choice between one of three: that I will make an enemy from other than them dominate over them, and he will despise them, or that I will I will either send famine upon them, or I will send death upon them, and they said: As for famine and enemy, we have no power with them, but death, So death was sent upon them, and seventy thousand of them died in one night. So I say: O God, by You I seek, by You I fight, and by You I fight.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8313","Muhammad ibn Uthman reported, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, who is Al-Aqdi, narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not hope to meet the enemy, for if you meet them, So be patient.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Yahya ibn Ma’in used to weaken al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He We looked into his hadith, and we did not find anything that indicated its weakness, and Yahya was more knowledgeable than us, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8314","Ziyad bin Yahya reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Zuhair, and Amr bin Yazid reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, he said: He told us Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, employed Abdullah bin Jubayr against the archers on the Day of Uhud. They were fifty men, and he said to them: “Be where you are, do not leave, and if you see birds, they will snatch us.” Al-Baraa said: I, by God, saw The women were displaying their anklets, their clothes loosened, as they ascended the mountain. When the matter was resolved, they went away. Abdullah bin Jubayr said: Their prince: How do you do what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says? So they departed, and that was what happened. When night fell, Abu Sufyan bin Harb came and said: Is Muhammad among you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not answer him.” Then he said: Is Muhammad among you? They did not answer him, then he said: Is Muhammad among you? The third time, but they did not answer him. He said: Is Ibn Abi Quhafa among you? They did not answer him, so he said: Is Ibn Abi Quhafa among you? They did not answer him until he said it three times, then he said: Is Ibn Al-Khattab among you? Until he said it three times, but they did not answer him, so he said: As for these, you have sufficed for them. Omar could not control himself, so he said: You lied, O enemy of God. Here is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and we are alive, and you have a bad day for us. He said: One day after the day of Badr. War is a dispute, and he said in the hadith of Ziyad, then he said: Come on Hubal, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Answer him,” and they said: What? We say, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Say: God is Most Mighty,” and in the hadith of Ziyad: God is Most High and Most Majestic. Then he said: “We have Uzza, and you have no Uzza,” so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace be upon him: “Answer him.” They said: O Messenger of God, and what do we say? He said: “Say: God is our Master, nor is He your Master.” Then Abu Sufyan said: You will see among the people an example that I did not command, then he said: “Why? \You make me feel bad\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8315","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Sumait told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: When We conquered Mecca, then we invaded Hunayn. He said: Then the polytheists came with the best arrays I had seen. He said: The horses arrayed, then the fighting array. Then the women were lined up behind that, then the sheep were lined up, then the camels were lined up. He said: And we are many human beings, we have reached six thousand. He said: And upon Khalid ibn al-Walid, avoiding our horses, said: It made our horses hide behind our backs. He said: It was not long before our horses were exposed, he said: So he called. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh, the immigrants.” Then he said: “O, the Ansar, oh the Ansar.” Anas said: This is the hadith of his aunt. He said: We said: At your command, O Messenger of God. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, advanced. By God, we did not come to them until God defeated them. He said: So we received that money, then we set off for Taif, where we besieged them for forty nights, then we returned to Mecca and camped, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gives a man a hundred, and he gives a man a hundred, brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8316","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Maqil bin Yassar, that Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “and it was when He did not fight at the beginning of the day. He delayed the fighting until the sun had set, the winds had blown, and victory had descended.”"
"8317","Muhammad bin Bashar told me, he said: Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Bara’, and a man asked him: Did you flee from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn? Al-Baraa said: “No, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not flee, so Hawazin were archers, and when we attacked them, they were defeated. So we focused on the spoils, and they attacked us with arrows, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his white mule. Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith took her bridle and said: “I am the Prophet. He is not lying. I am the son of Abdul Muttalib.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8318","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf told us, on the authority of Zuhair, and Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: he told us Abu Khaythamah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah ibn Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, he said: “We were in the hadith of Abbas when the fighting became hot,” and the other said: “When the battle is red, and the people meet the people, we will fear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for none of us will be closer to the people than he is.” The pronunciation is for Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8319","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Yusuf, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Haritha bin Mudharib, on the authority of Ali, who said: “We were dressed in white wool on the day of Badr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8320","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, saying: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever belongs to Ka’b bin Al-Ashraf, he has harmed God and His Messenger.” Muhammad bin Maslamah said: O Messenger of God, would you like Should I kill him? He said: “Yes.” He said: Permit me, so I may speak. He said: Say. So he came to him and said to him, and mentioned what had happened between them. He said: This man wanted Charity from us and he was stubborn to us, so when he heard it, he said: And also, by God, you will be bored with it. He said: We have followed it now, so we hate to leave it until we see it. How will his matter happen, and you wanted to give me an advance? He said: What will your women pledge to me? He said: You are the most beautiful of the Arabs. Should I pledge our women to you? ! He said: Will you mortgage your children with me? He said: He curses the son of one of us, so it is said: He pledged two wasqeen! But we will pledge to you the lamah, meaning the weapon. He said: Yes, so he promised him that he would come to him, God willing. So he set off with Abu Na’ila, and he was His infant, and his breast-feeding brother, and he set out with him Al-Harith, Abu Abbas bin Jabr, and Abbad bin Bishr. They came and called for him at night, so he disembarked. To them, Sufyan said: Other than Amr said: His wife said: I hear a sound as if it were the sound of blood. He said: This is Muhammad and his infant Abu Naila, if the noble man were called to a stabbing attack at night, he would respond. Muhammad said: If he comes, I will extend my hands to his head. I was able to see him without you, so when he came down, he came down dressed, and they said: We smell perfume from you, and he said: Yes, there is so-and-so below me, the most fragrant of women. The Arabs, he said: May I have permission to smell some of it? He said: Yes, then he sniffed. He said: Then he took it and smelled it. He said: Do you allow me to come back? He said: So he shook his head, then he said: Without you, he said: So they killed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8321","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, and he mentioned a word that means On the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Humayd bin Abdul Rahman told him that Umm Kulthum bint Uqba told him that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “He is not a liar who makes peace between people and then promotes good and says: good.” She said: I did not hear him make any concessions regarding anything. Lying about what people say except in three cases: in war, reconciliation between people, a man’s conversation with his wife, and a woman’s conversation with her husband. Umm Kulthum is one of the emigrants who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"8322","Muhammad bin Mansour and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “War is a deception.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8323","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id dictated to us in Nishapur. He said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Abu Kudaynah told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Sha`bi, on the authority of Stolen. He said: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib saying about something: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. I said: This is something I heard. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “War is a deception.”"
"8324","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, He said: Al-Hasan took one of the alms dates in his mouth, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Kush, kush, didn’t you realize that we were not eating?” \charity\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8325","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar told us, he said: I heard Thabit al-Bunani speaking, on the authority of Anas, he said: “When The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Khaybar. Al-Hajjaj bin Allat said: O Messenger of God, I have wealth in Mecca, and I have a family there, and I I want to come to them, so I am at liberty if I have permission from you, and I said something. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission. When he came to His wife in Mecca, he said to his family: Gather whatever money and whatever you have, for I want to buy from the spoils of the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And peace be upon him, and his companions, for they had been made unlawful, and their money had been gone, so the Muslims were subdued, and the polytheists showed joy and contentment.”"
"8326","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Muhammad bin Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Kathir bin Al-Abbas bin Abdul Al-Muttalib, on the authority of his father, said: On the day of Hunayn, the Muslims and the polytheists met, and the Muslims turned away that day, and I saw the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and no one was with him except Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib, taking the initiative of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, no. Oh, how quickly he ran towards the polytheists, so I went to him and took his bridle while he was on a gray mule, so he said: “O Abbas, call “The people of the brown,” and I was a man of good reputation, so I called out in my loudest voice: Where are the people of the brown? So they approached, as if they were camels when they longed for their children, saying: O Labayk, O Labayk, and the polytheists approached, so they met They and the Muslims, and the Ansar called out: O people of Ansar. Then the call was shortened for Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, so they called out: O My son. Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was riding his mule like a saddle, looked at their fight, and said: “This is when the heat The Battle.” Then he took some of the pebbles in his hand and threw them at them, then said: “They are defeated, by the Lord of the Kaaba. By God, I am still seeing their situation.” And he united them like a night until God defeated them. “It is as if I were looking at the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, running after them on his mule.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8327","Suleiman bin Ubaid Allah bin Amr told me, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Hashim told me, he is Yahya. Ibn Dinar Wasiti, on the authority of Abu Majliz, and he is Lahiq ibn Humayd, on the authority of Qais ibn Ubadah, on the authority of Abu Dharr in this verse: These two Two adversaries who disputed about their Lord. “This was revealed about those who dueled.”"
"8328","And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, he said: I heard Aba An atom swears an oath that this verse: These are two adversaries who disputed about their Lord. It was revealed about those who dueled on the day of Badr: Hamza and Ali. Ubaidah bin Al-Harith, Utbah, Shaybah ibn Rabi’ah, and Al-Walid bin Utbah."
"8329","Hilal bin Bishr told me, he said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Ubadah. On the authority of Ali, he said: “This verse was revealed about us, and during our duel on the day of Badr: These are two opponents who disputed about their Lord.”"
"8330","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, and Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Anas When the polytheists exhausted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was with seven of the Ansar and two men from the Quraysh, he said: “Who will turn away These people are on our behalf, and he is my companion in Paradise.” Then a man from the Ansar rose and fought until he was killed. When they were also exhausted, he said: “Who will turn these people away from me?” “And he is my companion in Paradise.” Until he killed seven, then he said to his companion: “We are not fair to our companions.”"
"8331","Hilal Ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Husayn Ibn Ayyash told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: He came A man masked in iron went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Do you think that if I had embraced Islam, would it have been better for me? He said: “Yes.” He said: He bore witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Then he said: O Messenger of God, did you see that if I were to My people, so I fought until I was killed, was it better for me, and I did not pray a prayer, except that I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that you are the Messenger of God? He said: “Yes.” He said: So he was attacked and killed, then they fought against him and he was killed. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He did an easy job and was rewarded.” “A lot.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: 5 Hussein bin Ayyash Ruqi Jazri, from the people of Bajda, trustworthy 5, 5 and Ali bin Ayyash Homsi, Trust 5 (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8332","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Many told me Ibn Abbas Ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: Abbas Ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: I witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Hunayn, so I committed I and Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not separate from him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted a white mule of his, given to him by Farwa bin Nafatha al-Jadami. When the Muslims and the infidels met, the Muslims turned away. They retreated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began running with his mule toward the infidels. Al-Abbas said: I was holding the bridle of the mule of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. She was restrained by the desire not to hasten, and Abu Sufyan was taking the passengers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “That is, Abbas, call the people of the tree.” Abbas said: I was a man of good reputation, so I said at the top of my voice: Where are the people of the tree? By God, it was as if I had compassion for them, when they heard my voice, the compassion of cows for their young, so they said: O Labbayk, O Labbaika, so they fought. They, and the infidels, and the call was among the Ansar, saying: O people of the Ansar. Then the call was limited to Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, so he looked The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was riding his mule as if he was straddling it to fight them, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is the time The battle became fierce.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took pebbles and threw them in the faces of the infidels, then said: “They are defeated, by the Lord of Muhammad.” \So I went to look"," and the fighting was as it was as it was narrated. By God"," it was nothing but the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," shot them. And he delivered his pebbles"," and I still see their limit blunt"," and their command withdrawn"," to the point that God defeated them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8333","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Zaid Al-Harawi told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadra On the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: And whoever turns his back to them on that day, he said: “It was revealed about the people of Badr.”"
"8334","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Bujayr, on the authority of Khalid, who is Ibn Ma’dan, he said: Abu Rahm al-Sama’i told me that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever dies worships God He does not associate anything with Him, performs prayer, pays zakat, fasts the month of Ramadan, and avoids great sins, for him is Paradise.” So he asked him what The major sins? He said: “Associating partners with God, killing a soul that God has forbidden, and fleeing on the Day of March.”"
"8335","Muhammad ibn al-Ala and Abdullah ibn Sa`id informed us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, who said: Shu`bah reported, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Assal, said: A Jew said to his friend: Take us to this prophet. His friend said: Do not call him a prophet. If he had heard you, he would have had four eyes. They came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about nine clear signs, and he said to them: “No.” Do not associate anything with God, and do not steal, and do not commit adultery, and do not kill the life that God has forbidden except in a just way, and do not lead an innocent to authority, and do not “Eat dawn, and do not consume usury, and do not slander a chaste woman, and do not flee on the day of the advance, and you, especially the Jews, must not violate the Sabbath.” So they kissed his hands and feet, and said: We bear witness that you are the Prophet of God. He said: What prevents you from following me? They said: David prayed that A prophet will be removed from his descendants, and we fear that if we follow you, you will kill us as Jews. The word is for Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8336","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Talha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he defeated a people, he would like to go down to their camp three times,” and he said again: “He would like to stay.” “By hitting them three times.”"
"8337","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has ordained goodness over all things, so if you kill So kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let each one of you sharpen his blade, and let his slaughtered animal rest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8338","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “I, Ammar, and Sa’d participated on the day of Badr, and Sa’d brought two captives, but I and Ammar did not bring anything.”"
"8339","Mukhlid bin Khaddash told us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, and Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer,” he said: “A word was omitted,” then he rode, and said: “God is great, Khaybar has been destroyed. “When we camped in the place of a people,” the morning of those who had been warned had arrived, and they came running through the city, saying: “Muhammad and Al-Khamis.” Then a messenger appeared. May God bless him and grant him peace. He killed their fighters and took their descendants captive, and Safiyya bint Huyay became Dihya al-Kalbi’s wife. Then She then became the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he married her and made her dowry for her emancipation. Abdul Aziz said to him: O Abu Muhammad, you. I asked Anas: What is her dowry? He said: Anas said: The most dowry is his freeing her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8340","Amr bin Mansour Abu Saeed Al-Nasa’i told us, trustworthy 5, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told me, he said: Sufyan bin Habib, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made The ransom of the people of pre-Islamic times on the day of Badr: four hundred. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8341","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, he said: Yahya bin Zakaria told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, On the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, he said: Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Badr, and said: “Be the best of your companions.” The captives, if they wished, could be killed, and if they wished, they could be ransomed, on the condition that a similar number of them be killed in the coming year. They said: “Redemption, and he will be killed from among us.” “And on the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, with (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8342","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Harb, whose surname was Turk, reported: Ali ibn al-Hussein ibn Waqid reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yazid the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a company. He said: They took spoils, and among them was a man. He said to them: I am not Among them, I fell in love with a woman, so I pursued her, so let me look at her for a moment, then do with me whatever you wish. He said: “And behold, a woman Long and bloody.” So he said to her: “Submit Hubaysh before you run out of food. I wonder if I followed you and caught up with you with a weapon or overtook you.” In the gorge, was it not right for a lover who took the trouble to insert the seeds and seeds to die? She said: Yes, I ransom you. He said: So they brought him forward and beheaded him. Then the woman came and stood over him, and she gasped for a breath or two, then she died. When they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, They told him the news, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is there not among you a merciful man?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8343","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, “He gave one man from the polytheists, and took two men from the Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8344","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Iyas bin Salamah bin told us Al-Akwa', that his father told him that he had fought with Abu Bakr, and he said: So we destroyed the polytheists, and our motto was, \Die"," die.\"" He said: So I killed. Seven verses in my hand"," so Abu Bakr sent me a woman from Banu Fazara"," one of the best Arabs"," so I brought her and met the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: “Give me the woman.” So I said: O Messenger of God"," by God"," I liked it"," and I did not like it. I revealed a dress to her"," then I met him after that in the market"," and he said: “O Salamah"," give me the woman for the sake of God"," your father.” I said: She is yours"," O Messenger of God"," so he took her and sent her to Mecca"," where he ransomed Muslim captives who were in the hands of the polytheists"," and she had a mother. \""with them\"""""
"8345","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Feed the hungry, minister to the sick, and free the oppressed.”"
"8346","Muhammad bin Nafi’ narrated, he said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated, on the authority of Anas, he said: It descended upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hudaybiyyah, eighty men from the people of Mecca came from Jabal al-Tanaim, and they said: We will take Muhammad and his companions. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took them in peace, then pardoned them. Then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: And it is He who withheld their hands from you and yours. \about them\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8347","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: I heard him. He narrates on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was prostrating while the leaders of Quraysh were sitting, and some camels were spread out. They said: Which of you will take this? He said: So they feared him, so Uqbah took him and threw him on his back, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him. And he bowed down, prostrating, and did not raise his head until Fatima came, took him from his back, and cursed what he had done. I saw him on that day calling On them, he said: “O God, bless Abu Jahl bin Hisham, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, Ubayyah, or Umayyah, and Uqba bin Abi Muayt. So I saw them killed on the day of Badr, and they were thrown away, except for an illiterate, for he was a huge man, and when he was dragged, he was cut into pieces.”"
"8348","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ja`far bin Aoun told us, Sufyan said: we told him on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying in the shade of the Kaaba, so Abu Jahl and some people from the Quraysh said: He Carrots were slaughtered in the vicinity of Mecca, so they sent and came from Salah, and they threw him between his shoulders, then Fatima came and threw it away from him, so when He left, and it was desirable for him to pray three times, so he said: “O God, be upon the Quraysh, O God, be upon the Quraysh, O God, be upon thee Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and Utbah.” Ibn Rabi’ah, Shaybah Ibn Rabi’ah, Umayyah Ibn Khalaf, and Uqba Ibn Abi Mu’it.” Abdullah said: I saw them killed. In the heart of Badr"
"8349","Amr bin Yazid reported, he said: Umayyah bin Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abd God, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, Abu Jahl was killed. He said: “Praise be to God, who has fulfilled his promise and strengthened his religion.”"
"8350","Yusuf bin Issa reported, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Jarir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Jarir, won’t you relieve me of Dhul-Khalasa?” He said: I ran away, and I was a man who was not able to ride horses, so he struck my chest with his hand, until I saw a mark. His fingers, and he said: “O God, make him steadfast, and make him a guide, a guided one.” So I burned them with fire, so Jarir sent a man from among us to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was called: Abu Artat. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, what I came to you until I left it as if it were a mangy camel. So he blessed Ahmose’s horses and their men five times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8351","Issa bin Muhammad Abu Umair told us, on the authority of Damra, on the authority of Al-Sibani, who is Yahya bin Abi Amr Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Dailami, on the authority of his father, said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the head of the lying lion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8352","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Ali Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Uqba Ibn Amir, that Amr Ibn Al-Aas and Sharhabeel Ibn Hasnah sent him a mail with the head of Yanaq Al-Batriq to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq. When he came to Abu Bakr with the head, he denied it, and said, O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, they are doing this to us. He said: “Should we please Persia and the Romans?! It is not acceptable.” “I have a solution, for only the Book and the News are sufficient for me.”"
"8353","Sulaiman bin Dawud and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us of a recitation by him, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, that Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Abi Rafi’ told him, that Abu Rafi’ told him, He received a letter from the Quraysh to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, put Islam into my heart, I said: O Messenger of God, by God I will never return to them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not betray a covenant, nor withhold cold, but go back. If what is in your heart is what is in your heart now, then go back.” So I returned to them, then I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So I converted to Islam. Bukair said: He told me that Abu Rafi’ was a Copt. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8354","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib, he said: It came out A man was riding a horse of his, meaning he was riding on it, and he passed by the mosque of Banu Hanifa, and their imam was reciting a Muslim recitation, so he referred that to Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masoud, so Abdullah sent to them, brought them, and asked them to repent, but they repented, except for Abdullah bin Al-Nawahah, and he was He was their imam, and Ibn al-Nawahah was killed, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If you were not a messenger, I would have beheaded you.” Today, you are not a messenger. Get up and behead him. So he got up and beheaded him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8355","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you were not a messenger, meaning a messenger, to Musaylimah, I would have killed you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8356","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Shuaib bin Harb told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign against him, so we camped at Batha’, and a Bedouin came. On his firstborn, so he whined and untangled his firstborn, and he saw tenderness among the people, so he returned to his firstborn, untied him, then mounted him, and a man from He greeted a she-camel of his, and I followed him. He was the one who greeted the virgin’s calf, and I was at the camel’s calf, so I preceded him. So I took hold of the firstborn’s cheek and said: Brother. When he sent his hands, I struck his neck. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills The man? They said: Salama bin Al-Akwa’. He said: “He has all his plunder.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8357","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Umamah narrates, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, that he heard him say that when the people of Qurayza came to the government of Sa’d, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came on a donkey. He said: “Indeed, these people came down to your ruling.” He said: “I rule that those who fight them should be killed and their descendants taken captive.” He said: “You have ruled over them.” \By the rule of the king\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8358","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: Sa’d bin Muadh was shot on the Day of Ahzab. So they cut off his ankle, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, crushed it with fire, and his hand swelled, so he let go of it, and blood bled out of him, so he cut it with another. His hand swelled, and when he saw that, he said: “O God, do not let me go out until my eyes are comforted by Banu Qurayza.” So he held his sweat and it did not drip. Drop by drop, until they came to the ruling of Saad bin Muadh, so he sent for him, and he ruled that their men should be killed, and their women should be spared, and he should seek help from them. Muslims, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have fulfilled the judgment of God over them,” and they were four hundred. When he finished killing them, His vein ruptured, and he died"
"8359","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Alqamah bin Marthad told me, that Suleiman bin Buraydah told him, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an emir to command an army or a company, he would call him and advise him. He bestowed good upon himself and the Muslims with him, and said: “Fight in the name of God, and do not deceive, and do not mutilate, and do not kill a child, and when You meet your enemy among the polytheists, so invite them to one of three, and if they respond to you, then accept from them, and desist from them. Invite them to Islam. If they do so, tell them that they have the same duties as the Muslims, and that they have the same duties as the Muslims, then call them to convert from Take their home to the home of the emigrants, and if they do so, tell them that they will have the same as the emigrants, and that they will have the same as the emigrants, for if they They converted to Islam and chose their homeland, so tell them that they are like the Bedouins of Muslims, and the judgment of God that applies to believers applies to them, or He said: On the Muslims, and they have nothing in the spoils or spoils, so if they refuse, then invite them to pay the tax. They did it, so accept from them, and desist from them. If they refuse, then seek help from God against them and fight them. And when you besiege a fortress, So they wanted to grant them the protection of God and the protection of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, but do not grant them the protection of God Almighty or the protection His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and assign to them your liability and the liability of your fathers and the liability of your companions, for if you conceal your liability, the liability Your companions, it is easier for you than to violate the protection of God Almighty and the protection of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. And when you besiege a fortress, So they wanted that you should bring them down to the rule of God, so do not put them down to the rule of God, for you do not know whether the rule of God is true in them or not, but Bring them down according to your rule.”"
"8360","Ahmad bin Hafs told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of my father Hassan Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Ashtar, that he narrated to him, that he said to Ali: “The people have become overwhelmed by what they hear, so if the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has made a covenant with you, so tell us about it. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has not entrusted me with a covenant that he did not make. To the people, except that in the bag of my sword was a sheet of paper, he said: “And behold, in it is that Abraham made Mecca sacred, and I make Medina sacred, and it is sacred between Its two deserts, no tree is cut from it except for fodder for a camel, and no weapon is carried in it for combat. And whoever commits an offense, it is upon himself, and whoever commits an offense shall be responsible for it. A juvenile, or he harbors a newly committed one, then the curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind is upon him. No retaliation will be accepted from him, nor will the justice of the believers be equaled. “Their blood will be shed, and the lowest of them will seek their protection, and they will be a hand against everyone else. No believer will be killed for an unbeliever, nor will he be able to keep a covenant with him.”"
"8361","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, He said: Al-Ashtar and I went to Ali and said: Did the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrust you with anything that he did not entrust to people in general? He said: No, except what is in this book of mine. So he took out a book from the scabbard of his sword, and lo and behold, in it was: “The believers, their blood will be repaid, and they will be dealt with.” Whoever is other than them, and the lowest of them will seek to fulfill their obligation. Is not a believer killed for an unbeliever, nor a covenant person during his covenant? And whoever commits an act should do so. himself, or gives shelter to an infidel, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all mankind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8362","Abu Al-Ash'ath told us, on the authority of Khaled, he said: Shu'bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “If the woman is generous to the Muslims,” and he said again: “If she is the newborn.”"
"8363","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Once, on the authority of her sister, she said: We hired two men from the polytheists who were my protectors, but my father’s son escaped upon them to kill them, so I said, “No.” You kill them until you start with me. So he left, and I said: Close the door for him. So I set off until I came to the hideout of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not find anything. I found him, and I found Fatima, and I said: Did you not see what I met from my father’s son? ! He did such-and-such to me, and she was harder on me than her husband, so she said: Do you support the polytheists? ! Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appeared upon me with a glow of dust, and said: “Welcome to Fakhta.” I said: O Messenger of God, did you not see what I encountered? Who is my father's son? ! I hired two father-in-laws of mine from the polytheists, and he wanted to kill them, so he said: “He has no right to do that. We have rewarded whomever you have rewarded, and we have protected whomever you have believed.” Then he said: “O Fatima, pour a bath for me,” so I poured it for him, so he bathed, then he prayed eight rak’ahs in one garment, with its two ends separated.”"
"8364","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a reading from him, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, On the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that Umm Hani, the daughter of Abu Talib, narrated to him, that she said: O Messenger of God, my mother’s son Ali claimed that he killed whom I hired! Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have rewarded whomever you have rewarded.”"
"8365","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Mukhlid told me, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I will expel the Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula until only a Muslim will remain therein.”"
"8366","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Between us In the mosque, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us and said: “Go to the Jews.” So we went out with him until we reached them, and he stood up. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O community of Jews, submit to Islam and you will be safe.” They said: You have conveyed the message, O Abu Al-Qasim. So he said to them: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “That is what I want. Submit and you will be safe.” They said: You have conveyed the message, O Abu al-Qasim. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them. May God bless him and grant him peace: “That is what I want.” Then he said the third time, and said: “Know that the land belongs to God and His Messenger, and that I want to evacuate you from This land, so whoever finds anything with his money, let him sell it. Otherwise, know that the land belongs to Allah and His Messenger.”"
"8367","Issa bin Hammad Zaghba told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah bin Al-Samit, On the authority of his father, that Ubadah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on hearing and obedience in times of hardship and ease, and on reviving. And compulsion, and not to dispute the matter with its people, and to uphold the truth wherever we are, not fearing the blame of the blamer.”"
"8368","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: “We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on hearing and obedience in times of hardship and ease, in things that are good and bad, and when things are good and bad. “And that we should not dispute the matter with those in charge of it, and that we should stand up for what is right wherever we are, not fearing the blame of the blamer.”"
"8369","Muhammad ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Sayyar Abi al-Hakam, and Yahya ibn Saeed Al-Qadi said that they heard Ubadah ibn Al-Walid speaking on the authority of his father. As for Sayyar, he said on the authority of his father: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for Yahya, he said: On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on hearing and obedience in our hardship. He pleases us, motivates us, compels us, and favors us, and that we do not dispute the matter with its people, and that we stand up for what is right wherever it is. We do not fear for the sake of God. “Blame Laim,” Shu’bah said: Sayyar did not mention this letter wherever it was, and Yahya mentioned it. Shu’bah said: If I added anything to it, It is on the authority of Sayyar, or on the authority of Yahya. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8370","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, and Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us upon hearing. And obedience in times of hardship and ease, when we are encouraged and when we are forced, and He has influence over us, and so long as we do not dispute the matter with its people, and so long as we say: In truth. \Wherever we are\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8371","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit informed me, he said: My father informed me, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: “We pledged allegiance The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to listen and obey in times of hardship and ease, in times of need and in times of compulsion, and not to dispute the matter with its people. And to speak or act according to the truth wherever we are, and not for God’s sake fear the blame of the blamer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8372","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Ubadah bin Al-Walid informed me, he said: My father informed me, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us on hearing and obedience in times of hardship and ease, in good times and in bad times, and not to dispute the matter.” its people, and that we stand up, or speak the truth, wherever we are, without fearing, for God’s sake, the blame of the blamer.”"
"8373","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, he heard Jabir say: “We did not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He greeted death, but we only pledged our pledge to him that we would not flee.”"
"8374","Abd al-Malik ibn Shuaib ibn al-Layth ibn Saad informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: Uqail narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Umayyah, that his father told him that Ya`la would be exalted. He said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Abu Umayyah. On the day of the conquest, I said: O Messenger of God, I pledge allegiance to my father on the emigration. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Rather, I pledge my allegiance to him on jihad.” “The migration has stopped.”"
"8375","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, That a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pledge allegiance to him to emigrate, and he said: I left my parents crying. He said: “Then go back to them. So make them laugh just as you made them cry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8376","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have come to pledge allegiance to you for migration, and I left my parents crying. He said: “Go back and make them laugh as you made them cry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8377","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, who is the son of Isa bin Al-Qasim bin Sami, he said: Zaid told us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah said that Abu Fatima told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You must emigrate, for there is no A similar example to her. He said: O Messenger of God, tell me something that I can do upright and do. He said: You must be patient, for there is no equal to it. He said: O Messenger of God, tell me knowledge that I can rely on and teach. He said: You must prostrate, for you do not prostrate to God in a prostration unless He raises you up. God has given you a degree, and He has removed from you any sin thereby.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8378","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid Al-Laythi, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that a Bedouin asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about immigration, and he said: “Woe to you, the matter of immigration is severe.” Do you have any camels? He said: Yes. He said: Will you pay your zakat? He said: Yes. He said: Work from across the seas, for God is blessed. And God Almighty will not leave out anything of your work.”"
"8379","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Mubashir bin Abdullah told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein told us, on the authority of Mu’alla bin Muslim, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, who said: Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and his companions The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were among the emigrants, because they abandoned the polytheists, and among the Ansar were emigrants, because Medina was a home. Shirk, so they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Aqaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8380","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Yusuf bin Issa informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who abandons what God has forbidden,” the wording given by Yusuf. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8381","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: A man said: O Messenger of God, which migration is best? He said: “To abandon what God hates, and migration is two migrations: the migration of the present, and the migration of the one who has begun. As for the one who is in the past, he obeys when commanded. He responds when he is called, and as for the one present: he is the greater of calamity and the better of reward.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8382","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of the Conquest: “No emigration, but jihad and intention, and if “If you are called out, then go out.”"
"8383","Muhammad bin Dawud told us, he said: Mu’alla bin Asad told us, he said: Wahib bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, said: I said: O Messenger of God, they say: No one will enter Paradise except those who emigrated. He said: “No.” Migration after the conquest of Mecca, but jihad with intention, and when you are mobilized, then mobilize.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8384","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Amr bin Al-Harith informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Amr bin Abd al-Rahman bin Umayyah bin Akhi Ya`la bin Munabbih told him that his father told him that Ya`la bin Umayyah said: I came to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon Abu Umayyah on the day of the conquest, so I said to him: O Messenger of God, pledge allegiance to my father on the emigration, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Rather, I pledge allegiance to him on the basis of jihad, and migration has ended.”"
"8385","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani, on the authority of Nu`aym bin Dajaja, he said: I heard Omar say: “There is no migration after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8386","Issa bin Musawar Al-Baghdadi told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Ala, he said: Busr bin Ubaid Allah told me, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Waqdan Al-Saadi, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a group of all of us. He asked for a need, and I was the last of them to enter the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: O Messenger of God, I left those behind me, and they They claim that the migration has stopped, so he said: “The migration will not stop as long as the infidels are killed.”"
"8387","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Marwan, meaning Ibn Muawiyah, told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Ala bin Zubr told us, he said: Busr bin Ubaid Allah narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Hassan bin Abdullah Al-Damri, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Saadi, he said: We visited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my companions entered and he fulfilled their needs. Then I was the last of them to enter and he said: “What do you need?” I said: O Messenger of God, when will the migration stop? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The migration will not stop as long as the infidels are killed.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Hassan bin Abdullah Al-Dhamri is not famous."
"8388","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, saying: Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Zubr, on the authority of Busr bin Ubaid Allah, On the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Hassan bin Al-Dhamri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Saadi, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. There was a group of people, all of us seeking a need, and I was the last of them to enter the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: O Messenger of God, I left behind... Behind me, and they claim that the migration has stopped, he said: “The migration will not stop as long as the infidels are killed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8389","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq and Ahmad bin Yusuf told me, saying: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Suleiman told me, he said: Busr bin Ubaid Allah narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Saadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Habib Al-Masry, he said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a group of people, all of us in need, so they came forward before him, and God judged for them on the tongue of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was upon him, may God bless him and grant him peace, whatever he wanted. Then I came to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “What is your need?” I said: I heard some of your companions saying: Migration has ceased. Shuaib said in his hadith. He said: Your need is one of the best of their needs. He said: Migration will not cease as long as the infidels are killed. And the pronunciation is for Ahmad. Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is Muhammad bin Habib, I do not know him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8390","Issa bin Musawar told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Hariz bin Uthman, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Awf, on the authority of Abu Hind Al-Bajli, said: Muawiyah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Migration does not stop until repentance stops, and Repentance will cease until the sun rises from the west.”"
"8391","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Hamzah, who said: Abu Alqamah Nadhar bin Alqamah told me, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Salama bin Nufayl, said: While I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came to him and said: O Messenger By God, the horses have been captured, the weapons have been laid down, and some people have claimed that there will be no fighting, and that the war has put an end to its effects. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “They lied. Now the fighting has come, and there will still remain from my nation a nation fighting in the way of God. Those who oppose them will not harm them. He deviates.” “God is the hearts of a people whom He provides for from among themselves. They fight until the Hour comes, and the war does not end until Gog and Magog emerge.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8392","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima bint Ruqaqiqa, She said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some women to pledge our allegiance to on Islam, and I said: O Messenger of God, shall we pledge our allegiance to you on the condition that we will not associate partners with you? We do not commit anything against God, nor do we steal, nor commit adultery, nor bring any slander that we invent between our hands and our feet, nor disobey you in what is right? He said: “As much as you are able and able,” so we said: God and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. Come, let us pledge our allegiance to you, O Messenger of God? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I do not shake hands with women, but my words to a hundred women are like my words to a woman, or the same as my words.” for one woman\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8393","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, Ibn Shihab said: Urwa bin Al-Zubair, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the believing women migrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He will be tested by God’s saying: O Prophet, when the believing women come to you. Aisha said: Whoever of the believing women acknowledges this has acknowledged this. By ordeal, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, acknowledged that from what they said, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: He said: “Go, for I have pledged allegiance to you.” By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never touched a woman except that he pledged his allegiance to them verbally. Aisha said: By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, never had anything to do with women except what God commanded him, and he used to say to them when He said to them: “I have pledged allegiance to you in words.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8394","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of a man, from the Al-Sharid family, called Amr, on the authority of His father, he said: “There was a leper in the Thaqif delegation, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him: “Go back, for I have pledged allegiance to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8395","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: A servant came and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. upon him and grant him peace upon the migration, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not feel that he was a slave, so his master came and wanted him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “With his own eyes,” so he bought him with two black slaves, then he did not pledge allegiance to anyone yet until he asked him: “Is he a slave?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8396","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told me, he said: Omar bin Yunus told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Al-Harmas bin Ziyad, he said: “ I extended my hand to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when I was a boy, so that he might pledge allegiance to me, but he did not pledge allegiance to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8397","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that an Arab swore allegiance to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a Bedouin fell ill in Medina, so the Bedouin came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: Oh Messenger of God, give me my pledge, but he refused. Then he came to him and said: Give me my pledge, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, refused, so the Bedouins left. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The city is only like a furnace; it expels its impurity, and its goodness is diffused.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8398","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Murrah talking, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The one who consumes usury, the one who pays it, the one who witnesses it, and the one who writes it down if they know that, and the one who gives usury, The woman who seeks beauty, the one who commits charity, and the apostate Arab after the Hijrah will be cursed, according to the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Judgment. \resurrection\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8399","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “It is the duty of a Muslim to listen and obey in whatever he likes or dislikes, unless he is ordered to commit a sin. If he is commanded to commit a sin, then it is not obligatory to listen to it.” And no obedience.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8400","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Zubaid Al-Ayami, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaida, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an army and ordered a man over them, so he lit a fire. So he said to them: Enter it. Some people wanted to enter it, and the others said: We just fled from it. So that was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He greeted, and said to those who wanted to enter it: “If you entered it, you would not cease to exist there until the Day of Resurrection,” and he said to the others, “Good,” and he said Ibn Al-Muthanna in his hadith: Well said, and he said: “There is no obedience in disobeying God, but obedience in what is right.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8401","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-A’mash, they heard Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Obedience is only in what is right.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8402","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Sayyar reported, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, he said: “I pledged allegiance The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me to listen and obey, so teach me what you are able to do, and advise every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8403","Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We used to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He praised listening and obedience, and He says to us: “As much as you are able.”"
"8404","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Umaima bint Ruqaqiqa, that she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us regarding women, and he said to us: “For what you are able and able to do.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8405","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ya’la bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas: O you who have believed, obey God and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. This was revealed about Abdullah bin Hudhafah bin Qais. Ibn Adi, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him on a mission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8406","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad told me, that Ibn Shihab told him, That Abu Salamah told him, that he heard, and Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu told him Bakr, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Muhammad, and Musa, who said: Ibn Shihab said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman said, I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God, and whoever obeys my prince has disobeyed God.” He obeyed me, and whoever disobeyed my prince disobeyed me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8407","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever obeys my prince has obeyed me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8408","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd, Lord of the Kaaba, He said: I came to Abdullah bin Amr while he was sitting in the shade of the Kaaba, and the people were gathered, so I heard him say: While we were with the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, when he descended at a certain place, and among us was someone who covered his tent, when his herald called: Prayer is unified, so we gathered. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and addressed us, saying: “There was no prophet before me, except that it was God’s duty to guide his nation.” on what he knows is good for them, and warns them of what he knows is bad for them, and that this nation of yours has been placed in its first state of health, and indeed Finally, calamity will befall them and things they will deny, temptation will come, and the believer will say: This is my destruction. Then it will be revealed, then it will come. temptation, so the believer says: This is this, then it is revealed, so whoever is pleased will be saved from the Fire and enter Paradise, Let his death overtake him, while he believes in God and the Last Day, and let him come to the people whom he would like to be brought to, and whoever pledges allegiance to an imam, So He gave him the touch of his hand and the fruit of his heart, so let him obey him as much as he is able.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8409","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Bahriyah, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Invasion is invasion: as for whoever seeks the face of God, He obeyed the imam, spent generously, and avoided corruption, for his sleep and his awakening will be rewarded in full. As for whoever invades out of hypocrisy and reputation, If he disobeys the Imam and spreads corruption on earth, he will not return with sufficient means.”"
"8410","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Jarir, he said: “I pledged allegiance to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May peace and blessings be upon him for advising every Muslim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8411","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Fayd, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, he said There was a treaty between Muawiyah and the Romans, so he wanted to travel through their country. When the time had passed, he raided them, and then a man A mule, saying: God is great, loyalty not treachery, then Amr bin Absa appeared, and Muawiyah asked him about his saying, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: “If there is a covenant between you and anyone, do not loosen a knot, and do not tighten it until its period has expired, or Reject them all the same.”"
"8412","Muhammad ibn Adam informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, “He accompanied a people of The polytheists, and he found among them negligent, so he killed them, and took their money, and brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he refused to \He accepts it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8413","Bishr ibn Khalid reported, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja’far reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever has four traits in him is a hypocrite, or one of the four traits in him is “There is a trait of hypocrisy in him until he abandons it: when he speaks he lies, when he makes a promise he breaks it, when he makes a covenant he betrays it, and when he disputes he commits ungodliness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8414","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and he mentioned on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: He said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No, for every traitor there is a banner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8415","Ali bin Hajar told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar told us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, saying: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, a banner will be erected for the treacherous person on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.”"
